      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the FDA maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is high, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Something else**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me that and add a note for the order, and I'll enter it as written. I'd still suggest confirming with pharmacy first."
      }
